Description: Pass PDF unchanged to driverless queues until there is a pdftopdf
 A queue made with `lpadmin -m everywhere` for a printer that accepts PDF
 gets the PPD line `*cupsFilter2: "application/vnd.cups-pdf application/pdf
 10 -"`, so a PDF job needs an application/pdf -> application/vnd.cups-pdf
 filter. CUPS 2.3 doesn't have one: pdftopdf comes from cups-filters, which
 NextBSD doesn't build yet, so cupsd refused PDF with "Unsupported
 document-format". Add a null ("-") filter for that step, as mime.convs
 already does for raw printing. cupsd drops null filters, and the ipp
 backend, seeing a PDF final content type, sends the job options (copies,
 sides, media, ...) for the printer to apply. What only pdftopdf does
 (number-up, page-ranges, fit-to-page done on the host) is not applied.
 The cost, 100, is above pdftopdf's 66, so cups-filters' line replaces this
 one once it is installed. Printers that take only PWG Raster or Apple
 Raster still need a rasteriser (cups-filters with Ghostscript or Poppler).
Origin: NextBSD
Forwarded: not-needed (Apple's CUPS is built only for macOS, which has its own PDF filters)
---
--- a/cups/conf/mime.convs.in
+++ b/cups/conf/mime.convs.in
@@ -35,6 +35,19 @@
 
 application/postscript		application/vnd.cups-postscript	66	pstops
 
+########################################################################
+#
+# PDF filters
+#
+# NextBSD doesn't ship cups-filters yet, so there is no pdftopdf. Driverless
+# (IPP Everywhere) queues for printers that accept PDF take
+# application/vnd.cups-pdf: pass PDF to them unchanged, and the ipp backend
+# sends the job options for the printer to apply. cups-filters' pdftopdf
+# (cost 66) takes over from this line once it is installed.
+#
+
+application/pdf			application/vnd.cups-pdf	100	-
+
 ########################################################################
 #
 # Raster filters...
